        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c773d0ad-7b1a-368b-be96-b2610969d0f0",
                "word": "leegroven",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ee73d830-ba53-3af1-8f51-69d4e71ae99b",
                        "entry_id": "c773d0ad-7b1a-368b-be96-b2610969d0f0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "inbreken en daarna alles plunderen wat er maar te plunderen valt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a504f941-9aed-4051-b24f-b9a69e506286",
                                "sense_id": "ee73d830-ba53-3af1-8f51-69d4e71ae99b",
                                "text": "12-jarige vast voor leegroven Arnhemse woning: Een 12-jarige jongen uit Arnhem is aangehouden omdat hij eind juli zou hebben ingebroken in een huis in zijn woonplaats. Ook drie andere verdachten uit Arnhem (16, 19 en 23 jaar oud) zijn gearresteerd na een onderzoek door de recherche."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e74892c3-27fc-4b2f-890c-027fe76f66f4",
                                "sense_id": "ee73d830-ba53-3af1-8f51-69d4e71ae99b",
                                "text": "Amine A. stond in zijn team Waddinxveen-Zuidplas bekend als een bloedfanatieke wijkagent. Maar volgens het Openbaar Ministerie leidde hij in elk geval van begin 2015 tot juni 2016 een dubbelleven. Hij zou informatie over tientallen hennepkwekerijen uit politiesystemen hebben doorgespeeld aan inbrekers. Die konden daardoor de boel leegroven voordat de politie binnenviel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13bbd1a5-5cd8-4bd2-bbe5-f33fa29a3b5b",
                                "sense_id": "ee73d830-ba53-3af1-8f51-69d4e71ae99b",
                                "text": "Ramkraken, waarbij criminelen met hun auto bij een supermarkt naar binnen rijden en de mobiele geldautomaten in de zaak leegroven, zijn ook weer minder populair. Na het nemen van extra beveiligingsmaatregelen waren er na vorige zomer nog maar vier ramkraken."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0d85dd2a-6632-4cd9-9a81-39f62cfed7ad",
                        "source_entry_id": "c773d0ad-7b1a-368b-be96-b2610969d0f0",
                        "source_sense_id": "ee73d830-ba53-3af1-8f51-69d4e71ae99b",
                        "target_lang_word": "loot",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loot",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5984f9e-6950-32a7-8b53-87f3eb902ab3",
                                        "entry_id": "3233b177-b1ea-3676-a9d8-5f9d0102a6f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of booty, goods seized from an enemy by violence, particularly (historical) during the sacking of a town in war or (video games) after successful combat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b355932-5141-4acc-b3f2-e4ea12ba6f1c",
                                                "sense_id": "c5984f9e-6950-32a7-8b53-87f3eb902ab3",
                                                "text": "Loot, plunder, pillage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eec84936-7bb6-41e8-ab92-890f70bbcecf",
                                                "sense_id": "c5984f9e-6950-32a7-8b53-87f3eb902ab3",
                                                "text": "He always found the talismanic gathering-word Loot (plunder), a sufficient bond of union in any part of India."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "432c6504-fe8e-410f-a8f7-3d8c042fff46",
                                                "sense_id": "c5984f9e-6950-32a7-8b53-87f3eb902ab3",
                                                "text": "Why, the race [of camp followers] is suckled on loot, fed on theft, swaddled in plunder, and weaned on robbery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb5ff9a5-463b-496e-9a90-2a0a24f6a2c1",
                                                "sense_id": "c5984f9e-6950-32a7-8b53-87f3eb902ab3",
                                                "text": "The horses in the archbishop's stables the murderers appropriated as their own fee,—or, as we should now say, as loot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bfdecce1-94be-4f98-bb35-b66db4dd1b4f",
                                                "sense_id": "c5984f9e-6950-32a7-8b53-87f3eb902ab3",
                                                "text": "But yet, with the persistent avariciousness of the white man, the Arabs clung to their loot, and when morning came forced the demoralized Manyuema to take up their burdens of death and stagger on into the jungle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "109396a6-c5d0-4acc-95f9-1e64fe061968",
                                                "sense_id": "c5984f9e-6950-32a7-8b53-87f3eb902ab3",
                                                "text": "India went from being a world-famous exporter of finished cloth into an importer, went from having 27% of world trade to less than 2%. Meanwhile, colonialists like Sir Robert Clive bought their rotten boroughs in England on the proceeds of their loot in India while taking the Hindi word \"loot\" into their dictionaries as well as their habits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef6ebe65-194c-4b4c-a8f8-c7307194cbc6",
                                                "sense_id": "c5984f9e-6950-32a7-8b53-87f3eb902ab3",
                                                "text": "The loot from the sack of Constantinople included the head of John the Baptist."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aec695a0-2cd9-3a64-b4ec-d7a8bb59ecc4",
                                        "entry_id": "3233b177-b1ea-3676-a9d8-5f9d0102a6f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of sack, the plundering of a city, particularly during war."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2c64160-2392-46bf-b640-349c8619de83",
                                                "sense_id": "aec695a0-2cd9-3a64-b4ec-d7a8bb59ecc4",
                                                "text": "He consented to the loot of the city by the men under his command."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db9b315c-090b-3c5c-b7a5-76add8bc8e12",
                                        "entry_id": "3233b177-b1ea-3676-a9d8-5f9d0102a6f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any valuable thing received for free, especially Christmas presents."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b56e1e57-75fc-4620-bf7f-a09fb0738926",
                                                "sense_id": "db9b315c-090b-3c5c-b7a5-76add8bc8e12",
                                                "text": "Free Loot for Children"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f1a9e24-4f89-37aa-9551-484d941c4ef1",
                                        "entry_id": "3233b177-b1ea-3676-a9d8-5f9d0102a6f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of money."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4a47089-7452-4644-83d4-6e4bcd3a1edb",
                                                "sense_id": "8f1a9e24-4f89-37aa-9551-484d941c4ef1",
                                                "text": "I got my mink the hard way. I paid for it. It cost a lot of loot and it took a little while to do it, but it's all mine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00280697-92b4-4a4c-8b35-eb532317c3bd",
                                                "sense_id": "8f1a9e24-4f89-37aa-9551-484d941c4ef1",
                                                "text": "There was nothing to do except for Mom to go back slaving away as somebody's maid. In Baltimore she couldn't make half the loot she could up North."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0613c1e7-b34e-4348-9a5f-4a8163770ecc",
                                                "sense_id": "8f1a9e24-4f89-37aa-9551-484d941c4ef1",
                                                "text": "How about all of those guys, dolls, dancers, fancy orchestration, and special lyrics? Didn't all of that cost a lot of loot? A good question. Would you believe me if I told you that we bought all of that talent for less than $10,000?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3137b66b-4f58-4f02-8dfb-b5ebf61c79ec",
                                                "sense_id": "8f1a9e24-4f89-37aa-9551-484d941c4ef1",
                                                "text": "Movies and TV were […] continuing to pretend for many years that the contents of a single briefcase could purchase a small country. Lately, though, filmmakers have made some sincere efforts to be realistic about the sheer bulk of pilfered loot)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "loot",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f27effe7-4bfb-33d5-8569-b86eff8b744b",
                                        "entry_id": "dd99b64e-9ac5-395d-8866-a64160abf430",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of plunder, to seize by violence particularly during the capture of a city during war or (video games) after successful combat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbada7ca-a043-418e-ba96-0b90bc573a6e",
                                                "sense_id": "f27effe7-4bfb-33d5-8569-b86eff8b744b",
                                                "text": "Gunganarian, the leader of the Chooars, continues his system of looting and murder"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9453b9bc-8c77-4dc9-8aff-98b0971ef88f",
                                                "sense_id": "f27effe7-4bfb-33d5-8569-b86eff8b744b",
                                                "text": "We looted the temple and the orphanage, which turned most of the NPCs against us."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89f0db38-bee1-497e-93ee-c1edb18c8368",
                                                "sense_id": "f27effe7-4bfb-33d5-8569-b86eff8b744b",
                                                "text": "The plunderers are beaten whenever they are caught, but there is a good deal of burning and ‘looting’ as they call it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b51875f6-1307-4001-a62e-78d11a911404",
                                                "sense_id": "f27effe7-4bfb-33d5-8569-b86eff8b744b",
                                                "text": "On the 22nd ultimo the Boers made a raid into the District, and the result was that some 300 head of cattle and 600 sheep were looted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc320309-d995-3b3d-a136-1baf9d23fd4d",
                                        "entry_id": "dd99b64e-9ac5-395d-8866-a64160abf430",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of rob, to steal something from someone by violence or threat of violence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64677d62-5ee7-47e0-bef6-6ea970e236b5",
                                                "sense_id": "bc320309-d995-3b3d-a136-1baf9d23fd4d",
                                                "text": "He told me... that if I gave him less than to the master of the luggage-boat, he would... declare at Shēr-Gurry that I had ‘looted him!’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
